# Group E — basic applications (item 39+).
# NOTE: --apt-recommends false (CLAUDE.md trap) — everything expected to
# come from Recommends is written here EXPLICITLY.

# --- File manager add-on (item 39; nemo is in 02-x11) ---
# nemo-fileroller: right-click compress/extract (pulls in file-roller).
# gvfs-backends/-fuse: SMB/SFTP/FTP/DAV shares + the fuse bridge; did not
# come with Recommends off, network shares would silently disappear.
nemo-fileroller
gvfs-backends
gvfs-fuse

# --- Archive formats (item 39: "archives COMPLETE" + fastest method) ---
# p7zip-full: 7z/cab/iso; unrar (non-free, firmware already opened
# non-free): rar extraction; zstd + pigz: fast multi-core compression.
p7zip-full
unrar
zstd
pigz

# --- Bulk rename (item 39) ---
# Multi-select + F2 → nemo calls the tool in the bulk-rename-tool key
# (zz-kavis.gschema.override). Mint's bulky is NOT in trixie.
gprename

# --- Right-click "copy path" (item 39) ---
# xclip for writing to the clipboard; the kavis action uses it.
xclip

# --- Editors (item 40) ---
# mousepad: fast, plain text editor (the notepad equivalent).
# kate: code/JSON editor — highlighting, folding, bracket matching ready;
# its settings in /etc/xdg/katerc. Pulls in the KF6/Qt6 stack; the ISO
# size is watched in CI (grup-e-taramasi.md).
mousepad
kate

# --- Disk and USB tools (item 42) ---
# gnome-disk-utility: formatting (NTFS/FAT/exFAT/ext4/btrfs, with short
# descriptions), SMART (udisks' built-in atasmart), "Restore Disk Image"
# = writing an ISO to USB (the Rufus equivalent).
# gparted: partitioning (item text "GParted installed").
# baobab: disk usage map (the WinDirStat equivalent).
# exfatprogs: exFAT formatting/repair support.
gnome-disk-utility
gparted
baobab
exfatprogs
# smartmontools: the disk health check in Settings > Hardware test
# (item 50). Without it that check can only say "no data", which on a
# machine with a dying disk is the wrong answer.
smartmontools

# --- Printer and scanner (item 43) ---
# The first path is DRIVERLESS (grup-e-taramasi): modern printers speak
# IPP Everywhere — cups-browsed + avahi show the network ones by
# themselves, ipp-usb bridges a USB printer to the same protocol; most
# users never see a driver screen. The wizard is system-config-printer
# (auto discovery + driver + test page; writing our own wizard is
# against the install-and-configure rule). gutenprint fallback for old
# devices. The CUPS web interface (631) is localhost-only by default.
# Scanner: sane-airscan (driverless eSCL/WSD) + the simple-scan UI.
cups
cups-browsed
cups-filters
avahi-daemon
ipp-usb
system-config-printer
printer-driver-gutenprint
sane-airscan
simple-scan

# --- Terminal conveniences (item 44) ---
# command-not-found + apt-file: package suggestion on an unknown command
# (the database is built at build time in the 0240 hook). gettext-base:
# terminal-tips.sh's translations (the gettext command).
command-not-found
apt-file
gettext-base

# --- Web browser (4C: Firefox as the pinned default) ---
# firefox-esr: maintained in Debian — security patches come from apt, no
# version jumps. l10n-tr: the product's first language is Turkish.
firefox-esr
firefox-esr-l10n-tr

# --- Safe USB use (item 63) ---
# psmisc: fuser — to say which application is holding a USB stick that
# cannot be removed.
psmisc
